# Reaction Based Support and Resistance Zones

- url: https://www.tradingview.com/script/C8si1UZX-Reaction-Based-Support-and-Resistance-Zones/
- type: indicator
- pine_id: PUB;d53e3684f666427aad3d6eaebd373837
- version: 1.0

## Description

## Overview

Reaction Based Support and Resistance Zones is a visual price-action study tool for reaction-based horizontal zones and local reaction levels.

The script is designed to show where price has recently reacted, how those reactions are grouped into zones, and how the same reaction context can be studied both in the current live chart and in historical visible-range views.

It does not generate trading signals. It does not provide entries, exits, targets, stops, position sizing, win rate, or performance claims.

## What it shows

This script can display:

- Live reaction zones based on confirmed pivot reactions.
- Support-like, resistance-like, mixed, and inactive reaction roles.
- Touch count, freshness, ATR-normalized reaction strength, width penalty, and a visual zone score.
- Visible Range Research context for historical chart study.
- Local Window Levels across the visible historical window.
- A compact dashboard with neutral context information.
- Neutral live alerts for confirmed reaction-zone events.

The displayed zones and local levels are historical reaction context. They are not predictions.

## Context modes

The script includes three context modes:

### Live

Live context shows the current reaction-zone state at the latest bars. This is the normal current-chart view. Live context can extend active zones to the right for readability.

Live is the only context that can trigger alerts.

### Visible Range Research

Visible Range Research reconstructs the reaction context as it existed at the right edge of the currently visible chart range.

This mode is intended for historical visual study. When the user scrolls or zooms the chart, the research view recalculates for that visible range.

Visible Range Research does not trigger alerts.

### Auto Hybrid

Auto Hybrid is the default mode.

When the latest bars are visible, the script uses Live context. When the chart is scrolled back into historical data, the script switches to Visible Range Research.

## How it works

The script uses confirmed pivot highs and confirmed pivot lows as reaction events.

A support-like reaction is based on a confirmed pivot low. A resistance-like reaction is based on a confirmed pivot high.

Nearby reactions are clustered into reaction zones. Each zone stores information such as:

- center price
- zone width
- first and last reaction
- touch count
- support-like and resistance-like reaction counts
- average and maximum reaction strength
- invalidation state
- visual quality information

Zones are scored using a configurable combination of touch count, freshness, ATR-normalized reaction strength, width penalty, quality information, and invalidation state.

Only confirmed pivots are used. Unconfirmed pivot points are not displayed.

## Local Window Levels

Visible Range Research includes a local-window layer built directly from confirmed pivot reactions.

Local Window Levels are independent from the right-edge context zones. This means smaller reactions on the left, center, or right side of the visible historical chart can remain visible even if they later become part of a broader context zone.

Local Window Levels can:

- appear on the left, center, or right side of the visible chart
- start and end inside the visible window
- continue from the visible left edge if they already existed at that point
- end before the visible right edge
- show smaller historical reaction areas that may not be obvious from broader zones alone

This behavior is intentional. The local layer is for historical visual study, not for prediction.

## Local detection quality

The local layer includes quality controls for confirmed pivot reactions.

Balanced Quality is the default profile. It is designed to reduce obvious noise while still keeping useful local reaction context visible.

Exploratory shows more local reactions for broader visual study.

Strict and Very Strict reduce the number of local levels by requiring stronger reaction quality.

Local reaction quality can consider:

- ATR-normalized reaction distance
- wick or close-away validation
- local pivot prominence
- same-swing duplicate suppression
- short-term local clustering

Line density is controlled before a local level is confirmed. Confirmed local levels are not hidden merely for visual clarity in the rendering stage unless a hard object limit or explicit user setting applies.

## Historical visual study

In Visible Range Research, local levels are drawn relative to the currently visible chart window.

A local level does not need to extend to the visible right edge.

Short lines, mid-window lines, and lines that end before the right side of the chart are normal. They show where local reaction areas existed during that historical view.

This mode helps users study how reaction areas formed, continued, changed, or stopped being relevant across past market structure.

## Dashboard

The dashboard provides compact context information, including:

- current view context
- active zone count
- nearest lower reaction zone
- nearest upper reaction zone
- highest zone score
- last confirmed reaction age
- detection status

The dashboard uses neutral wording. It does not recommend any trading action.

Dashboard text size, backdrop strength, position, and right-side spacing are adjustable for readability near the price scale.

## Alerts

Alerts are live-context event notifications only.

Available alert events include:

- New reaction zone confirmed
- Existing reaction zone updated
- Price touched an active reaction zone
- Reaction zone became inactive
- Reaction zone reactivated after a confirmed reaction

Visible Range Research rendering does not trigger alerts.

## How to use it

Use this script as a visual context tool for price areas where confirmed historical reactions have occurred.

Possible study uses include:

- observing recent reaction zones in Live context
- reviewing how reaction areas formed in past visible chart windows
- comparing broader reaction zones with smaller Local Window Levels
- adjusting detection quality profiles to fit the symbol and timeframe
- keeping the chart clean while still preserving reaction context

The default settings are starting points, not optimized settings.

## Limitations

Reaction zones and local levels are historical context, not forecasts.

A reaction area can stop reacting at any time.

Pivot-based events appear only after confirmation, so there is a natural confirmation delay.

Visible Range Research recalculates when the chart is scrolled or zoomed.

Lower timeframes and highly volatile symbols can produce more local levels.

Strict settings may remove useful reactions. Exploratory settings may show more lines.

This is a visual study tool, not a strategy or backtest engine.

## Non-repaint explanation

The script uses confirmed pivot highs and confirmed pivot lows only.

A pivot reaction is processed only after the required pivot-right confirmation bars have passed.

Unconfirmed pivots are not displayed.

The script does not use request.security() with lookahead.

Visible Range Research reconstructs the reaction context using only the information available up to the visible right edge.

Scores and visual states can update as new confirmed bars become available, but this is based on confirmed historical data and does not use future data relative to the active context.

## What this script does not do

This script does not generate trading signals.

It does not provide entries, exits, targets, stops, position sizing, win rate, or performance claims.

It does not predict future price movement.

It does not simulate orders.

It is not a strategy.

It is not a backtest system.

It is not financial advice.

## 日本語補足

このインジケーターは、価格が実際に反応した水平帯を可視化するための研究用ツールです。

Liveでは最新状態の主要な反応ゾーンを表示します。

Visible Range Researchでは、過去にスクロールした表示範囲の右端時点を基準に、当時存在していた反応コンテキストを再構築します。

Local Window Levelsは、表示範囲内の確定pivot反応から作られる局所的な反応ラインです。左側、中央、右側に出る短い線や、右端まで伸びない線は仕様です。過去相場の中で、どこに細かい反応帯が存在したかを研究するためのものです。

ライン数は、描画側で検知済みのものを隠して減らすのではなく、検知品質やローカルクラスタリングによって調整します。

このスクリプトは売買シグナルではありません。エントリー、エグジット、利確、損切り、ポジションサイズ、勝率、収益性、将来予測を提供しません。投資助言ではありません。

## Source Code

````pine
//@version=6
indicator("Reaction Based Support and Resistance Zones", shorttitle="Reaction SR Zones", overlay=true, max_boxes_count=500, max_lines_count=500, max_labels_count=500)

// ============================================================================
// Reaction Based Support and Resistance Zones
// Auto-detects recent price-reaction support/resistance candidate bands and
// draws them as managed horizontal price zones. Confirmed pivot reactions are
// clustered into zones, scored for importance, and only the top few are shown.
// Price series only. No repainting: only confirmed pivots are used.
// ============================================================================

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// INPUT GROUP: Detection
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
gDet = "Detection"
pivotLeft              = input.int(3, "Pivot Left", minval=1, maxval=20, group=gDet, display=display.none)
pivotRight             = input.int(3, "Pivot Right", minval=1, maxval=20, group=gDet, display=display.none)
reactionLookbackBars   = input.int(500, "Reaction Lookback Bars", minval=100, maxval=5000, group=gDet, display=display.none)
atrLength              = input.int(14, "ATR Length", minval=1, maxval=200, group=gDet, display=display.none)
minReactionAtr         = input.float(0.20, "Min Reaction (ATR)", minval=0.0, maxval=5.0, step=0.05, group=gDet, display=display.none)
useWickFilter          = input.bool(true, "Use Wick Filter", group=gDet, display=display.none)
minWickToBodyRatio     = input.float(0.50, "Min Wick To Body Ratio", minval=0.0, maxval=10.0, step=0.1, group=gDet, display=display.none)
useBodyDirectionFilter = input.bool(false, "Use Body Direction Filter", group=gDet, display=display.none)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// INPUT GROUP: Zone Width
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
gWidth = "Zone Width"
zoneWidthMode   = input.string("ATR", "Zone Width Mode", options=["ATR", "Percent", "Ticks"], group=gWidth, display=display.none)
zoneAtrMult     = input.float(0.25, "Zone ATR Mult", minval=0.01, maxval=5.0, step=0.01, group=gWidth, display=display.none)
zonePercent     = input.float(0.10, "Zone Percent", minval=0.01, maxval=5.0, step=0.01, group=gWidth, display=display.none)
zoneTicks       = input.int(20, "Zone Ticks", minval=1, maxval=10000, group=gWidth, display=display.none)
maxZoneWidthAtr = input.float(1.50, "Max Zone Width (ATR)", minval=0.10, maxval=10.0, step=0.1, group=gWidth, display=display.none)
minZoneTicks    = input.int(5, "Min Zone Ticks", minval=1, maxval=1000, group=gWidth, display=display.none)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// INPUT GROUP: Clustering
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
gClust = "Clustering"
mergeMode          = input.string("Overlap", "Merge Mode", options=["Overlap", "Center Distance"], group=gClust, display=display.none)
mergeAtrMult       = input.float(0.50, "Merge ATR Mult", minval=0.01, maxval=5.0, step=0.01, group=gClust, display=display.none)
maxStoredZones     = input.int(40, "Max Stored Zones", minval=5, maxval=100, group=gClust, display=display.none)
preferSameRoleMerge = input.bool(true, "Prefer Same Role Merge", group=gClust, display=display.none)
allowMixedZones    = input.bool(true, "Allow Mixed Zones", group=gClust, display=display.none)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// INPUT GROUP: Scoring
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
gScore = "Scoring"
minTouchesToShow      = input.int(2, "Min Touches To Show", minval=1, maxval=10, group=gScore, display=display.none)
minScoreToShow        = input.int(30, "Min Score To Show", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gScore, display=display.none)
freshnessHalfLifeBars = input.int(120, "Freshness Half Life Bars", minval=10, maxval=2000, group=gScore, display=display.none)
touchWeight           = input.int(35, "Touch Weight", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gScore, display=display.none)
freshnessWeight       = input.int(25, "Freshness Weight", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gScore, display=display.none)
rejectionWeight       = input.int(25, "Rejection Weight", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gScore, display=display.none)
widthPenaltyWeight    = input.int(15, "Width Penalty Weight", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gScore, display=display.none)
invalidatedScoreMult  = input.float(0.35, "Invalidated Score Mult", minval=0.0, maxval=1.0, step=0.05, group=gScore, display=display.none)
qualityWeight         = input.int(10, "Quality Weight", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gScore, display=display.none)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// INPUT GROUP: Detection Quality (additive event-quality layer; visual only)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
gQual = "Detection Quality"
detectionEngine        = input.string("Quality Weighted", "Detection Engine", options=["Classic", "Quality Weighted"], group=gQual, display=display.none)
reactionStrengthMode   = input.string("Hybrid", "Reaction Strength Mode", options=["Post-Pivot Range", "Close Away", "Hybrid"], group=gQual, display=display.none)
minEventQualityScore   = input.int(35, "Min Event Quality Score", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gQual, display=display.none)
usePivotProminenceFilter = input.bool(true, "Use Pivot Prominence Filter", group=gQual, display=display.none)
minPivotProminenceAtr  = input.float(0.10, "Min Pivot Prominence (ATR)", minval=0.0, maxval=5.0, step=0.05, group=gQual, display=display.none)
useCloseAwayFilter     = input.bool(false, "Use Close-Away Filter", group=gQual, display=display.none)
minCloseAwayAtr        = input.float(0.10, "Min Close-Away (ATR)", minval=0.0, maxval=5.0, step=0.05, group=gQual, display=display.none)
minEventSeparationBars = input.int(3, "Min Event Separation Bars", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gQual, display=display.none)
sameSwingHandling      = input.string("Update Only", "Same-Swing Handling", options=["Count Normally", "Update Only", "Ignore"], group=gQual, display=display.none)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// INPUT GROUP: Historical Research (additive research-depth layer; visual only)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
gHist = "Historical Research"
researchMaxStoredZones = input.int(120, "Research Max Stored Zones", minval=40, maxval=300, group=gHist, display=display.none)
preserveHistoricalResearchZones = input.bool(true, "Preserve Historical Research Zones", group=gHist, display=display.none)
researchArchivePruneMode = input.string("Archive Friendly", "Research Archive Prune Mode", options=["Score Freshness", "Archive Friendly"], group=gHist, display=display.none)
researchShowArchiveZones = input.bool(true, "Research Show Archive Zones", group=gHist, display=display.none)
researchArchiveTransparency = input.int(94, "Research Archive Transparency", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gHist, display=display.none)
researchMinArchiveScore = input.int(20, "Research Min Archive Score", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gHist, display=display.none)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// INPUT GROUP: In-Window Detail (Research-only local reaction segments; visual)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
gInWin = "In-Window Detail"
showInWindowDetail = input.bool(true, "Show In-Window Detail", group=gInWin, display=display.none)
// DEFAULT CHANGE: the legacy event-segment / lifecycle-trail layers are now
// opt-in COMPARISON layers (default "Off"). The Local Window Levels engine
// (see the inputs further below) is the primary historical-detail layer.
inWindowDetailMode = input.string("Off", "In-Window Detail Mode", options=["Off","Segments Only","Segments + Right-Edge Zones"], group=gInWin, display=display.none)
maxInWindowSegments = input.int(45, "Max In-Window Segments", minval=5, maxval=120, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
maxSegmentsPerWindowBucket = input.int(15, "Max Segments Per Window Bucket", minval=1, maxval=40, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
inWindowSegmentSelection = input.string("Balanced Left Center Right", "Segment Selection", options=["Balanced Left Center Right","Score Only","Recent Within View"], group=gInWin, display=display.none)
inWindowSegmentExtensionBars = input.int(80, "Segment Extension Bars", minval=5, maxval=1000, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
inWindowSegmentMinScore = input.int(20, "Segment Min Score", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
inWindowSegmentMinQuality = input.int(20, "Segment Min Quality", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
inWindowSegmentUseFill = input.bool(false, "Segment Use Fill", group=gInWin, display=display.none)
inWindowSegmentTransparency = input.int(78, "Segment Transparency", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
inWindowSegmentLineWidth = input.int(1, "Segment Line Width", minval=1, maxval=3, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
inWindowSegmentStyle = input.string("Dotted", "Segment Style", options=["Solid","Dotted","Dashed"], group=gInWin, display=display.none)
showInWindowSegmentLabels = input.bool(false, "Show Segment Labels", group=gInWin, display=display.none)
inWindowSegmentLabelMode = input.string("Tiny", "Segment Label Mode", options=["Tiny","Compact"], group=gInWin, display=display.none)
// Lifecycle Trails (additive Research-only detail engine; visual only). Trails
// show WHERE a local reaction zone existed DURING the visible window: they can
// start left/center, end mid-window when the zone died or changed state, and
// are never extended by future data.
inWindowDetailEngine = input.string("Lifecycle Trails", "In-Window Detail Engine", options=["Event Segments","Lifecycle Trails","Both"], group=gInWin, display=display.none)
researchCompositionMode = input.string("Lifecycle Detail + Context Zones", "Research Composition", options=["Lifecycle Detail + Context Zones","Lifecycle Detail Only","Event Detail + Context Zones","Event Detail Only","Right-Edge Context Only"], group=gInWin, display=display.none)
maxLifecycleTrails = input.int(80, "Max Lifecycle Trails", minval=10, maxval=180, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
maxTrailsPerWindowBucket = input.int(25, "Max Trails Per Window Bucket", minval=3, maxval=60, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
lifecycleTrailSelection = input.string("Balanced Left Center Right", "Trail Selection", options=["Balanced Left Center Right","Score Only","Duration Then Score"], group=gInWin, display=display.none)
lifecycleTrailStartPolicy = input.string("Actual Origin Or Visible Left", "Trail Start Policy", options=["Actual Origin","Actual Origin Or Visible Left"], group=gInWin, display=display.none)
lifecycleTrailEndPolicy = input.string("Until Invalidation Or State Change", "Trail End Policy", options=["Fixed Bars","Until Invalidation Or State Change","Until Research Right Edge"], group=gInWin, display=display.none)
lifecycleTrailMaxBars = input.int(250, "Trail Max Bars", minval=10, maxval=3000, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
lifecycleStateChangeAtr = input.float(0.35, "Trail State Change (ATR)", minval=0.05, maxval=5.0, step=0.05, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
lifecycleMinDurationBars = input.int(3, "Trail Min Duration Bars", minval=1, maxval=100, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
lifecycleMinScore = input.int(15, "Trail Min Score", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
lifecycleMinQuality = input.int(15, "Trail Min Quality", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
lifecycleShowInactiveTrails = input.bool(true, "Show Inactive Trails", group=gInWin, display=display.none)
lifecycleTrailTransparency = input.int(72, "Trail Transparency", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
lifecycleInactiveTransparency = input.int(88, "Inactive Trail Transparency", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
lifecycleTrailLineWidth = input.int(1, "Trail Line Width", minval=1, maxval=3, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
lifecycleTrailStyle = input.string("Dashed", "Trail Style", options=["Solid","Dotted","Dashed"], group=gInWin, display=display.none)
showLifecycleTrailLabels = input.bool(false, "Show Trail Labels", group=gInWin, display=display.none)
lifecycleTrailLabelMode = input.string("Tiny", "Trail Label Mode", options=["Tiny","Compact"], group=gInWin, display=display.none)
researchContextZoneTransparencyBoost = input.int(8, "Context Zone Transparency Boost", minval=0, maxval=30, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
// Visible Window Local S/R Engine ("Local Window Levels"): the PRIMARY
// historical-detail layer. It is built DIRECTLY from confirmed pivot reaction
// events and is fully independent of the right-edge research zone (rZone)
// model, so small left-side/center reactions stay visible even when the rZone
// path merged or ignored the same event. Visual study only; no alerts.
historicalDetailEngine = input.string("Local Window Levels", "Historical Detail Engine", options=["Local Window Levels","Right-Edge Context Only"], group=gInWin, display=display.none)
// DEFAULT CHANGE: "Local Levels Only" — the right-edge context zones are now
// OPT-IN for research (choose "Local Levels + Muted Context" to compare).
localWindowMode = input.string("Local Levels Only", "Local Window Mode", options=["Local Levels Only","Local Levels + Muted Context","Muted Context Only"], group=gInWin, display=display.none)
showLocalWindowLevels = input.bool(true, "Show Local Window Levels", group=gInWin, display=display.none)
// Local Detection Profile: drives the escalation of local reaction-quality
// gates. "Exploratory" accepts every confirmed pivot (1 pivot = 1 candidate,
// all confirmed) to show the raw picture; "Balanced Quality" applies the tuned
// defaults (and the localRespect* fine-tune switches); "Strict Quality" and
// "Very Strict Quality" progressively raise the reaction / event-quality /
// validation / prominence floors so fewer, higher-quality local levels are
// confirmed. Visual study only; never affects Live or alerts.
localDetectionProfile = input.string("Balanced Quality", "Local Detection Profile", options=["Exploratory","Balanced Quality","Strict Quality","Very Strict Quality"], group=gInWin, display=display.none)
// Local reaction-quality inputs (fine-tune the Balanced profile; the profile
// escalates their effective floors). Visual study only.
localMinEventQuality = input.int(35, "Local Min Event Quality", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
localValidationMode = input.string("Wick Or Close-Away", "Local Validation Mode", options=["Reaction Only","Wick Or Close-Away","Wick And Close-Away"], group=gInWin, display=display.none)
localMinWickToBodyRatio = input.float(0.40, "Local Min Wick To Body", minval=0.0, maxval=10.0, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
localMinCloseAwayAtr = input.float(0.12, "Local Min Close-Away (ATR)", minval=0.0, maxval=5.0, step=0.05, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
localUseProminenceFilter = input.bool(true, "Local Use Prominence Filter", group=gInWin, display=display.none)
localMinProminenceAtr = input.float(0.10, "Local Min Prominence (ATR)", minval=0.0, maxval=5.0, step=0.05, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
localMinEventSeparationBars = input.int(4, "Local Min Event Separation Bars", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
localSameSwingPolicy = input.string("Merge Same Swing", "Local Same-Swing Policy", options=["Allow All","Merge Same Swing","Ignore Same Swing"], group=gInWin, display=display.none)
localClusterConfirmMode = input.string("Cluster Or Strong Single", "Local Cluster Confirm Mode", options=["Any Accepted Event","Cluster Or Strong Single","Cluster Only"], group=gInWin, display=display.none)
localMinClusterReactions = input.int(2, "Local Min Cluster Reactions", minval=1, maxval=10, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
localStrongSingleQuality = input.int(70, "Local Strong Single Quality", minval=0, maxval=100, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
localPreloadBars = input.int(2000, "Local Preload Bars", minval=0, maxval=5000, group=gInWin, display=display.none)
// Preload filter: "Overlap Window" keeps every level overlapping the visible
// window (the start-bar cutoff is skipped); "Start Within Preload" keeps the
// legacy start-bar cutoff (start >= visible left - preload bars).
